issue.body:
A route registered with a RegExp that has the `g` (or `y`) flag only matches every other request. `RegExp#exec` on such a regexp starts from `lastIndex` and moves it forward after a match, and the layer keeps the same regexp object across requests, so the next request starts matching from the old position and fails.

```js
const router = new Router()
router.get(/^\/u\/(\d+)$/g, (req, res) => res.end(JSON.stringify(req.params)))
// GET /u/1 -> 200 {"0":"1"}
// GET /u/2 -> 404
// GET /u/3 -> 200 {"0":"3"}
// GET /u/4 -> 404
```

Expected: every request returns 200, the same as without the flag.

The regexp matcher in `lib/layer.js` now sets `lastIndex` to 0 before calling `exec`, so each match starts at the beginning of the path. The flag is otherwise left alone.

Tested with a new case in `test/router.js` that requests `/foo`, `/zoo`, `/foo` against `/^\/[a-z]oo$/g`. On master it fails with `Error: expected 200 "OK", got 404 "Not Found"` on the second request. With the change, `npm test` (827 passing), `npm run lint` and `npm run test-types` pass.

